{
 "about": "Every Microsoft Graph call TenantKeep On-Call makes, for the daily Graph change watch. A test fails when a Kit adds a Graph path that is not listed here. smoke is the read the live check makes against the Kainor tenant; null means schema check only. requires names the tenant-wide plan a live read needs (P1, P2, Intune, Defender); the live check skips it when GW_TENANT_FEATURES does not list it, and the schema and changelog checks still cover it. Nothing here ever reads a password, a recovery key or a pass. {deviceUserId} in a smoke read is the primary user of a managed device, found at run time, because Intune answers 404 for a person it does not know. hunting lists the advanced hunting tables and columns the Email tab's fixed queries use (SecurityKit/EmailHunting.swift); the live check compiles a zero-row projection of each, so a renamed column fails without reading any mail.",
 "calls": [
  {
   "id": "inventory.devices",
   "requires": [
    "Intune"
   ],
   "kit": "InventoryKit",
   "method": "GET",
   "version": "v1.0",
   "path": "/deviceManagement/managedDevices",
   "select": [
    "id",
    "deviceName",
    "managedDeviceName",
    "operatingSystem",
    "osVersion",
    "azureADDeviceId",
    "userPrincipalName",
    "userDisplayName",
    "emailAddress",
    "serialNumber",
    "model",
    "manufacturer",
    "complianceState",
    "lastSyncDateTime"
   ],
   "smoke": "/deviceManagement/managedDevices?$top=1&$select=id,deviceName,managedDeviceName,operatingSystem,osVersion,azureADDeviceId,userPrincipalName,userDisplayName,emailAddress,serialNumber,model,manufacturer,complianceState,lastSyncDateTime"
